Rationale: release 1.1.2 treats a function's nominal duration as its maximum
single-shot audio duration. Feature extraction adds 0.02 seconds, so exact
15.000-second PCM requests a 15.02-second encoder input and cannot use the only
configured 15-second Core ML function. The downstream patches expose the
existing 239,600-sample (14.975-second) usable window capacity and cap
single-shot planning to that capacity, routing longer inputs through the
existing windower without changing decoding or word-timing behavior.

Reproduce the recorded hashes from this directory with:

  shasum -a 256 Sources/PhononCoreML/Transcriber.swift \
    Sources/PhononCoreML/Windower.swift Binaries/libPhononTDT.a

Reproduce upstream source hashes by replacing each vendored Swift path with the
corresponding file from the pinned release and commit above.
